{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778550735,"nonce":"62EnEpG0I8Luf1JaayKBkf8v6i8=","message":"**Fix implemented** on `feature/fix-rebuild-splash-race` (36e8373).\n\n**Root cause:** The health poll in `app.tsx` checked only whether `/api/health` returned 200. During a self-merge rebuild, the daemon broadcasts `mandible:rebuilding` SSE, then runs post-merge hooks (including `npm run build`, which takes 10-30s), then schedules `process.exit(0)` after 500ms. The health poll starts 3s after the SSE event — while the daemon is still alive during the build step. The first poll succeeds, triggers `window.location.reload()`, which resets `rebuilding` to `false`, and the user sees the auth page with no daemon behind it.\n\n**Fix (3 layers):**\n1. **Server:** `AuthQueue._rebuilding` flag is set before broadcasting the SSE event. The `/api/health` endpoint includes `rebuilding: true` in the response when this flag is set.\n2. **Client:** Health poll now parses the response JSON and skips reload if `data.rebuilding === true`. Only reloads when the NEW daemon instance responds (which won't have the rebuilding flag).\n3. **Cleanup bug:** The inner `setInterval` cleanup was returned from the `setTimeout` callback (dead code — the return value of a setTimeout callback is discarded). Refactored to track `intervalId` in the outer scope so the `useEffect` cleanup can clear it.\n\n**Files changed:** `src/types.ts`, `src/auth-queue.ts`, `src/server.ts`, `src/index.ts`, `ui/src/app.tsx`","files":null}]}